IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-15: Article 15 (accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. The Omnibus did not change Article 15.
-- Every function that concerns a system takes the date asked, the AI system and the harmonisation facts and answers through the gate of P2-section-2-gate.l4: NOTHING when Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 do not apply to the system on the date asked,
-- JUST FALSE where Article 2(2) cuts the Article off, NOTHING where Article 2(13) says it may be limited. Reading a result: JUST TRUE the requirement is met; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered.
-- Paragraph 2 is a duty of the Commission and concerns no system: it takes no gate (fork F-commission-no-gate). Qualifiers inside a limb ("where appropriate", "as appropriate") are folded into the limb's yes or no (fork F-qualifier-fold).

§ `Article 15(1): an appropriate level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity`

-- src:365 | 1. High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed in such a way that they achieve an appropriate level of accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity, and that they perform consistently in those respects throughout their lifecycle.
@ref Art 15(1) (src:365)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it achieves an appropriate level of accuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it achieves an appropriate level of robustness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it achieves an appropriate level of cybersecurity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it performs consistently in those respects throughout its lifecycle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1) the high-risk AI system achieves an appropriate level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity and performs consistently` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 15, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it achieves an appropriate level of accuracy` AND `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it achieves an appropriate level of robustness` AND `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it achieves an appropriate level of cybersecurity` AND `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it performs consistently in those respects throughout its lifecycle`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed in such a way that they achieve an appropriate level of accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity, and that they perform consistently in those respects throughout their lifecycle"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 15(2): the Commission and benchmarks`

-- src:366 | 2. To address the technical aspects of how to measure the appropriate levels of accuracy and robustness set out in paragraph 1 and any other relevant performance metrics, the Commission shall, in cooperation with relevant stakeholders and organisations such as metrology and benchmarking authorities, encourage, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies.
@ref Art 15(2) (src:366)
-- A duty of the Commission: no AI system and no date gate (fork F-commission-no-gate); no seat (an official). "as appropriate" is folded into the second fact.
GIVEN `the Commission has acted in cooperation with relevant stakeholders and organisations such as metrology and benchmarking authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has encouraged, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies to address the technical aspects of how to measure the appropriate levels of accuracy and robustness set out in paragraph 1 and any other relevant performance metrics` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(2) the Commission has encouraged the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies` MEANS
    JUST (`the Commission has acted in cooperation with relevant stakeholders and organisations such as metrology and benchmarking authorities` AND `the Commission has encouraged, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies to address the technical aspects of how to measure the appropriate levels of accuracy and robustness set out in paragraph 1 and any other relevant performance metrics`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall, in cooperation with relevant stakeholders and organisations such as metrology and benchmarking authorities, encourage, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies"


§ `Article 15(3): declared levels of accuracy`

-- src:367 | 3. The levels of accuracy and the relevant accuracy metrics of high-risk AI systems shall be declared in the accompanying instructions of use.
@ref Art 15(3) (src:367)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the levels of accuracy of the high-risk AI system are declared in the accompanying instructions of use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant accuracy metrics of the high-risk AI system are declared in the accompanying instructions of use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(3) the levels of accuracy and the relevant accuracy metrics are declared in the accompanying instructions of use` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 15, "", 3)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the levels of accuracy of the high-risk AI system are declared in the accompanying instructions of use` AND `the relevant accuracy metrics of the high-risk AI system are declared in the accompanying instructions of use`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The levels of accuracy and the relevant accuracy metrics of high-risk AI systems shall be declared in the accompanying instructions of use"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


