-- src:369 | The robustness of high-risk AI systems may be achieved through technical redundancy solutions, which may include backup or fail-safe plans.
@ref Art 15(4) second subparagraph (src:369)
-- A liberty ("may be achieved", "may include"): JUST TRUE where the means named is used; NOTHING where another means is used (silent).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the robustness of the high-risk AI system is achieved through technical redundancy solutions, which may include backup or fail-safe plans` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(4) second subparagraph the robustness may be achieved through technical redundancy solutions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 15, "", 4)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the robustness of the high-risk AI system is achieved through technical redundancy solutions, which may include backup or fail-safe plans`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may be achieved through technical redundancy solutions, which may include backup or fail-safe plans": a liberty; the text neither requires this means nor excludes others
        ELSE JUST (TRUE)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:370 | High-risk AI systems that continue to learn after being placed on the market or put into service shall be developed in such a way as to eliminate or reduce as far as possible the risk of possibly biased outputs influencing input for future operations (feedback loops), and as to ensure that any such feedback loops are duly addressed with appropriate mitigation measures.
@ref Art 15(4) third subparagraph (src:370)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system continues to learn after being placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is developed in such a way as to eliminate or reduce as far as possible the risk of possibly biased outputs influencing input for future operations (feedback loops)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is developed in such a way as to ensure that any such feedback loops are duly addressed with appropriate mitigation measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(4) third subparagraph the high-risk AI system that continues to learn is developed to eliminate or reduce the risk of feedback loops` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 15, "", 4)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system continues to learn after being placed on the market or put into service`)
