-- src:373 | The technical solutions to address AI specific vulnerabilities shall include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for attacks trying to manipulate the training data set (data poisoning), or pre-trained components used in training (model poisoning), inputs designed to cause the AI model to make a mistake (adversarial examples or model evasion), confidentiality attacks or model flaws.
@ref Art 15(5) third subparagraph (src:373)
-- The list of attacks is joined by "or" but is read as five matters the measures cover, each where appropriate (fork F-15-5-list): "shall include" gives the minimum.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for attacks trying to manipulate the training data set (data poisoning)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for attacks trying to manipulate pre-trained components used in training (model poisoning)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for inputs designed to cause the AI model to make a mistake (adversarial examples or model evasion)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for confidentiality attacks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for model flaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(5) third subparagraph the technical solutions to address AI specific vulnerabilities include measures against the listed attacks` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 15, "", 5)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for attacks trying to manipulate the training data set (data poisoning)` AND `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for attacks trying to manipulate pre-trained components used in training (model poisoning)` AND `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for inputs designed to cause the AI model to make a mistake (adversarial examples or model evasion)` AND `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for confidentiality attacks` AND `the technical solutions include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for model flaws`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The technical solutions to address AI specific vulnerabilities shall include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for attacks ..."
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Regulative rule of Article 15(2)`

DECLARE `Art 15(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 15(2) encourage, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies`

-- src:366 | 2. To address the technical aspects of how to measure the appropriate levels of accuracy and robustness set out in paragraph 1 and any other relevant performance metrics, the Commission shall, in cooperation with relevant stakeholders and organisations such as metrology and benchmarking authorities, encourage, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies.
@ref Art 15(2) (src:366)
-- "the Commission shall, in cooperation with ... encourage, as appropriate": a duty of the Commission with no time limit and no consequence stated: no breach path. The Commission's duty is not tied to one AI system (fork F-commission-no-gate).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 2(13) body` `Art 15(2) act`
`Art 15(2) the Commission's duty to encourage the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies` MEANS
    PARTY Commission
    MUST `Art 15(2) encourage, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies`
    HENCE FULFILLED
